{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_memory_decisions_adr_0002_no_actor_entity_exists_in_the_schema_by_construc_no_actor_entity", "label": "ADR-0002: No Actor Entity Exists in the Schema, By Construction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/memory/decisions/ADR-0002-no-actor-entity-exists-in-the-schema-by-construc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TRIGGERS: adding an actors table, claiming two contexts are two operators, joining contexts. The schema has request, mint, sighting and a context identifier, with no actor table and no join that would produce one. The product's claim is bounded by its data model rather than by a disclaimer in the copy. The earlier framing that false positives were 'bounded by HMAC collision' was FALSE \u2014 the HMAC bounds token provenance, not actor distinctness \u2014 and must never be reintroduced. Governs canarymaze/schema.sql and canarymaze/detect.py."}, {"id": "docs_memory_decisions_adr_0002_no_actor_entity_exists_in_the_schema_by_construc_741_address_actor_label_measurement", "label": "741-Address Actor Label Measurement", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/memory/decisions/ADR-0002-no-actor-entity-exists-in-the-schema-by-construc.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One actor label in the organizers' own collusion.wiki dump spans 741 distinct addresses (stored_revisions 899 / stored_revision_ips 741). The measured fact behind the no-actor-entity decision, the scope limit line, and the demo's unhappy-path beat."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_memory_decisions_adr_0002_no_actor_entity_exists_in_the_schema_by_construc_no_actor_entity", "target": "architecture_detect_py", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/memory/decisions/ADR-0002-no-actor-entity-exists-in-the-schema-by-construc.md", "sourc